have
an MC=3 armor on but I do appreciate the folks who think displacement
is worth the difference of MC=2.

> Was it smart of me to not even bother with my longsword?

Yes, but.  Yes because there are more long sword artifacts than
any other type and long sword is one of the best melee types.
But because Valks can best to Expert in long sword and for
melee Exert is a trap.  It is *very* wasteful of skill slots to become
expert in anything melee at the expense of multifire capability in
any missile type.  Use the long sword as a backup to thrown
daggers throughout the game.  Whether to switch to a wielded
dagger, I've done it both ways and I think the extra damage of
the long sword matters.

> I'm wondering
> if maybe I shouldn't just use the long sword some from the start(try
> to get an Excalibur asap), and try to throw my dagger as often as the
> opportunity arises(to raise skill). I'm not sure though...the few
> games I have started exclusively with the dagger, I never really had
> any issues not being able to kill things in melee(at least in the
> stages of the game I have made it to).

The problem comes in with monsters that are strong relative to
your current hit points.  Whacking with the long sword while
retreating towards the up stairs can make a big difference
compared to whacking with a dagger while retreating towards
the up stairs.  Killing one more monster in an advancing hoard
can mean surviving to get upstairs to heal.

> Will Mjollner work throughout the whole game? It seems like a solid
> weapon, but I'm wondering if I shouldn't be looking for something
> better later(I haven't made it to the "later" stages, but I'm just
> wondering for the future).

It blows up items carried by monsters.  It's the best artifact in
the early game but by the late game that becomes a problem.
Lawfuls can have Excalibur and when playing lawfuls I get that
and ignore Mojo.  With neutrals it's a harder tradeoff.  I certainly
would not spend the skill slots to move it to expert until all other
slots you ever plan to spend have been.  With Mojo the difference
between skilled and expert is small.

